# *arr compatibility APIs

External apps (Overseerr, Bazarr, LunaSea) call these routes as if they were upstream. Response shapes, field names, and status codes follow Sonarr v3, Radarr v3, and Prowlarr v1.

- Routers: `internal/api/compat/sonarr`, `radarr`, `prowlarr`. Each is an `http.Handler` switching on a normalized path.
- Mounts in `cmd/replacearr`: `/sonarr/` scope `sonarr`, `/radarr/` scope `radarr`, `/prowlarr/` scope `prowlarr`.
- Contract notes: `docs/discovery/01-sonarr-v3-compatibility.md`, `02-radarr-v3-compatibility.md`, `03-prowlarr-v1-compatibility.md`. Confirm payloads against `.tmp/Sonarr` (`src/Sonarr.Api.V3`), `.tmp/Radarr` (`src/Radarr.Api.V3`), and `.tmp/Prowlarr` (`src/Prowlarr.Api.V1`). Do not modify `.tmp/`. Update the matching discovery note when a compat route changes.
- Prowlarr also serves Torznab/Newznab at `/prowlarr/{indexerId}/api` with `t=caps`, `t=search`, `t=tvsearch`, and `t=movie`.
- Compat handlers share the unified store. A series created via `/sonarr/api/v3/series` must appear on the native API, and the reverse.
- Quality ids, protocol strings (`torrent`, `usenet`), and resource field names stay aligned with upstream. Add a case to the existing path switch and a test in `internal/api/compat/compat_test.go`.

```go
// BAD: native-only field names on a Sonarr route
writeJSON(w, http.StatusOK, map[string]any{"tvdbId": id, "showName": s.Title})

// GOOD: Sonarr v3 resource names
writeJSON(w, http.StatusOK, map[string]any{"tvdbId": id, "title": s.Title})
```
